Fix a finite set $\Phi\subset[0,1]\cap\mathbb Q$ and an integer $1\leq d\leq4$. There are positive integers $p_0\mid p$, with $p_0$ clearing $\Phi$, and a rational DCC set $\mathcal B\subset[0,1]$, depending only on $d$ and $\Phi$, with the following property. Suppose $(X,B)$ is a projective lc pair of dimension $d$ with coefficients in $\Phi$, and $$f:X\longrightarrow Z,\qquad \dim Z>0,\qquad K_X+B\sim_\mathbb Qf^*D,$$ where $f$ is a contraction and $D$ is a rational Cartier divisor. There exist $\psi\in\mathbb C(X)^*$ and $D_Z\sim_\mathbb QD$ such that $$\label{eq:relative-exact-presentation}
 K_X+B+\frac{1}{p_0}\mathop{\mathrm{Div}}(\psi)=f^*D_Z,
 \qquad D_Z=K_Z+B_Z+M_Z.$$ Here $B_Z$ is effective with coefficients in $\mathcal B$, the pair $(Z,B_Z+M_Z)$ is generalized lc, and $\mathbf M$ is b-nef with $p\mathbf M$ b-Cartier. If $(X,B)$ is klt, the generalized pair is generalized klt.

Fix a finite set $\Phi\subset[0,1]\cap\mathbb Q$ and a positive integer $p_0$ clearing its denominators. There is a positive integer $p$, depending only on $\Phi$ and $p_0$, divisible by $p_0$, with the following property. Let $$f\colon N\longrightarrow C$$ be a projective contraction from a normal integral variety to a smooth complex curve, let $c\in C$, and suppose $1\leq\dim N\leq4$. Set $F=f^*[c]$ and $T=F_{\mathrm{red}}$. Assume that $N$ is $\mathbb Q$-factorial, that $(N,T+H)$ is dlt, and that $H$ is an effective horizontal $\mathbb Q$-divisor with coefficients in $\Phi$. Suppose, on a neighbourhood of $F$, that there are $\beta\in\mathbb Q$ and $\psi\in\mathbb C(N)^*$ such that the following is an equality of actual $\mathbb Q$-divisors, for a fixed canonical divisor: $$\label{eq:slc-local-relation}
 p_0(K_N+T+H)+\mathop{\mathrm{Div}}\psi
       =p_0\beta F.$$ Then $p\beta\in\mathbb Z$.
